Object.assign(T.en,{"bv_else": "Elsewhere, a blank vote has effects", "bvh_h": "Blank vote: yes, no, and what it changes", "bvh_p": "Every country profile has a “Voting” tab: how to vote in practice, the electoral system, turnout and, as we roll it out, what a blank vote changes. The rules differ a lot from one country to the next:", "bvh_cards": [["France", "Counted separately and published, but with no effect on the result or on thresholds."], ["Spain", "Counted as a valid vote: it raises the 3% bar that gives access to seats. Only an empty envelope is blank."], ["Colombia", "If it wins a majority, the election is held again, without the same candidates."], ["Peru", "Above two thirds of blank or spoilt votes, the election is annulled."]], "bvh_note": "Blank or spoilt? A word or a crossing-out on the paper usually makes the vote spoilt. Check your country's rules before voting.", "bvh_go": "See the blank vote in France"});
